'''Pablo Barrios Rivas''' (born 15 June 2003) is a Spanish professional [[Association football|footballer]] who plays as a [[midfielder]] for [[La Liga]] club [[Atlético Madrid]] and the [[Spain national football team|Spain national team]].

==Club career==
Barrios began his youth career in [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]] before moving to their city rivals, [[Atlético Madrid]], in 2017.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://okdiario.com/deportes/barca-quiere-pablo-barrios-joya-cantera-del-atletico-9222351 |title=El Barça quiere a Pablo Barrios, la joya de la cantera del Atlético |date=11 June 2022 |website=OkDiario |language=es |access-date=30 October 2022 |archive-date=30 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221030020652/https://okdiario.com/deportes/barca-quiere-pablo-barrios-joya-cantera-del-atletico-9222351 |url-status=live }}</ref> He became a central part of the club's [[Atlético Madrid (youth)|under-19 team]] in the 2021–22 season, which reached the semi-finals in the [[UEFA Youth League]] for the first time in the club's history.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.football-espana.net/2022/03/03/who-is-atletico-madrids-latest-starlet-pablo-barrios |title=Who is Atletico Madrid's latest starlet Pablo Barrios? |first=Alan |last=Feehely |date=3 March 2022 |website=Football España |access-date=30 October 2022 |archive-date=30 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221030020536/https://www.football-espana.net/2022/03/03/who-is-atletico-madrids-latest-starlet-pablo-barrios |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 3 March 2022, Barrios signed his first professional contract with ''Atleti'', keeping him until 2025.<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.mundodeportivo.com/futbol/atletico-madrid/20220303/1001759584/pablo-barrios-contrato-2025-convocado-simeone-levante.html |title=Pablo Barrios, contrato hasta 2025 y convocado por Simeone ante el Levante |date=3 March 2022 |website=[[Mundo Deportivo]] |language=es |access-date=30 October 2022 |archive-date=25 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221225203555/https://www.mundodeportivo.com/futbol/atletico-madrid/20220303/1001759584/pablo-barrios-contrato-2025-convocado-simeone-levante.html |url-status=live }}</ref> In the 2022–23 season, he advanced to playing for the [[Atlético Madrid B|reserve team]], but was soon called up to the first team, making his professional [[La Liga]] debut on 29 October as a second half [[Substitute (association football)|substitute]] to [[Geoffrey Kondogbia]] in a 3–2 away loss against [[Cádiz CF]].<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://www.eldesmarque.com/madrid/atletico-de-madrid/noticias-2/259261-quien-es-pablo-barrios-el-real-madrid-echo-al-ultimo-debutante-del-atletico-de-madrid-de-simeone |first=Joaquín |last=Anduro |title=¿Quién es Pablo Barrios? El Real Madrid echó al último debutante del Atlético de Madrid de Simeone |date=29 October 2022 |website=ElDesmarque |location=Madrid |language=es |access-date=30 October 2022 |archive-date=30 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221030020718/https://www.eldesmarque.com/madrid/atletico-de-madrid/noticias-2/259261-quien-es-pablo-barrios-el-real-madrid-echo-al-ultimo-debutante-del-atletico-de-madrid-de-simeone |url-status=live }}</ref>

Barrios scored his first goal for ''Atleti'' on 22 December 2022, netting his team's second in a 3–1 away victory against [[CD Arenteiro]], for [[2022–23 Copa del Rey|the season]]'s [[Copa del Rey]].<ref>{{Cite news |first=Francisco Javier |last=Díaz |title=Gol histórico de Pablo Barrios |url=https://as.com/futbol/copa_del_rey/gol-historico-de-pablo-barrios-n/ |newspaper=[[Diario AS]] |date=22 December 2022 |access-date=14 September 2025 |language=es |archive-date=24 December 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221224121000/https://as.com/futbol/copa_del_rey/gol-historico-de-pablo-barrios-n/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> His first professional goal came on 4 January 2023, as he scored the second of Atlético's 2–0 victory at [[Real Oviedo|Oviedo]] in the same tournament.<ref>{{Cite news |first=Víctor |last=Delgado |title=Así hemos contado la victoria del Atlético de Madrid sobre el Real Oviedo |url=https://elpais.com/deportes/2023-01-04/real-oviedo-atletico-de-madrid-en-directo-los-dieciseisavos-de-la-copa-del-rey-en-vivo.html |newspaper=[[El País]] |date=4 January 2023 |access-date=14 September 2025 |language=es |archive-date=30 November 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251130050821/https://elpais.com/deportes/2023-01-04/real-oviedo-atletico-de-madrid-en-directo-los-dieciseisavos-de-la-copa-del-rey-en-vivo.html |url-status=live }}</ref>

On 25 January 2023, Barrios renewed his contract until 2028, and was officially promoted to the main squad, being assigned the number 24 jersey.<ref>{{Cite news |url=https://as.com/futbol/copa_del_rey/pablo-barrios-ya-es-del-primer-equipo-llevara-el-dorsal-24-n/ |title=Pablo Barrios ya es del primer equipo: llevará el dorsal '24' |trans-title=Pablo Barrios already is a first team member: will wear the number '24' jersey |newspaper=Diario AS |publisher=[[PRISA]] |language=es |date=25 January 2023 |access-date=31 January 2023 |archive-date=3 April 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20230403191832/https://as.com/futbol/copa_del_rey/pablo-barrios-ya-es-del-primer-equipo-llevara-el-dorsal-24-n/ |url-status=dead }}</ref> After the departure of fellow ''Atleti'' youth product [[Saúl (footballer, born 1994)|Saúl]] in the 2024–25 season, he was given his number 8 jersey, and further consolidated his position as a starter in [[Diego Simeone]]'s squad.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Villarreal 2-2 Atlético |url=https://www.espn.com/soccer/lineups/_/gameId/704669 |publisher=[[ESPN]] |date=19 August 2024 |access-date=31 August 2024 |archive-date=28 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260428044441/https://www.espn.com/soccer/lineups/_/gameId/704669 |url-status=live }}</ref>{{Better source needed|date=September 2025}}

==International career==
Barrios is a youth international for Spain, having debuted for the [[Spain national under-19 football team|under-19 team]] in 2022.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://as.com/futbol/2022/03/02/champions/1646260342_667327.html |title=Pablo Barrios, el héroe del Atlético con pasado blanco |first=Sergio |last=Picos |date=2 March 2022 |website=Diario AS |language=es |access-date=30 October 2022 |archive-date=30 October 2022 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20221030020800/https://as.com/futbol/2022/03/02/champions/1646260342_667327.html |url-status=live }}</ref> He was also a member of the [[Spain national under-23 football team|Spain under-23]] squad that won a gold medal in football at the [[Football at the 2024 Summer Olympics – Men's tournament|2024 Paris Summer Olympics]].<ref name="olympics2024"/> Due to injuries of [[Martín Zubimendi]] and [[Álex Baena]], Barrios received his first senior international call-up in November 2024 for a [[2024–25 UEFA Nations League A]] match against [[Switzerland national football team|Switzerland]],<ref>{{Cite web |url=https://cadenaser.com/nacional/2024/11/16/pablo-barrios-encuentra-su-oportunidad-con-la-roja-cadena-ser/ |website=[[Cadena SER]] |title=Pablo Barrios encuentra su oportunidad con 'La Roja' |date=16 November 2024 |language=es |access-date=16 November 2024 |archive-date=22 April 2026 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20260422044851/https://cadenaser.com/nacional/2024/11/16/pablo-barrios-encuentra-su-oportunidad-con-la-roja-cadena-ser/ |url-status=live }}</ref> debuting on 18 November in the same match.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Pablo Barrios debuta con España en una noche inolvidable |url=https://onefootball.com/es/noticias/pablo-barrios-debuta-con-espana-en-una-noche-inolvidable-40325364 |website=[[OneFootball]] |date=18 November 2024 |access-date=14 September 2025 |language=es |via=atleticosport.es |archive-date=15 October 2025 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20251015224258/https://onefootball.com/es/noticias/pablo-barrios-debuta-con-espana-en-una-noche-inolvidable-40325364 |url-status=live }}</ref>

